--- a/CHANGES
+++ b/CHANGES
@@ -29,6 +29,16 @@ Version 3.3.3 - in development
 ------------------------------
 - Adding support for Python 3.15.
 
+- Fixed `QuotedString` silently discarding white space in its quote delimiters, so
+  that `QuotedString("\n;", multiline=True)` behaved like `QuotedString(";")`.
+  White space in `quote_char` and `end_quote_char` is now kept as part of the
+  delimiter (the sequence must still contain at least one non-whitespace
+  character, so an all-whitespace quote char still raises `ValueError`). If
+  `quote_char` starts with white space, those characters are dropped from the
+  expression's skippable whitespace so the opening quote can actually be matched,
+  and a non-`multiline` `QuotedString` whose end quote contains a line end no
+  longer matches across lines. Issue #492.
+
 - Fixed `pyparsing_common.as_datetime` raising `Invalid date/time: microsecond
   must be in 0..999999` for valid ISO-8601 timestamps whose fractional seconds
   round up to a full second (e.g. `2021-06-15T12:30:59.9999995`, common in
